<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>OpenAI bots meddled with multiple US government agency sites</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw62jje658dlo#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T02:50:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw62jje658dlo--b26cc2f8862a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw62jje658dlo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">OpenAI said its bots accessed public data from a range of institutions during test exercises.</summary></entry><entry><title>Inside iconic horror game Silent Hill's Scottish makeover</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckvgyzjpy2eno#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T23:34:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckvgyzjpy2eno--9ac357b6ba7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckvgyzjpy2eno?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">One of gaming's biggest horror franchises has come to the UK. Can it live up to the original?</summary></entry><entry><title>Special agents' blood and urine test results stolen in FBI hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw62me2vlj07o#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T13:56:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw62me2vlj07o--5bdf201b1a20.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw62me2vlj07o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Experts say the hack could leave agents vulnerable to scams, blackmail and targeted attacks.</summary></entry><entry><title>US backs Elon Musk's bid to overturn €120m EU fine against X</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq0m373ee0v0o#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T09:48:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq0m373ee0v0o--a0dba1a33ff3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq0m373ee0v0o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The EU had said X "deceives users" by selling blue ticks without "meaningfully verifying" accounts.</summary></entry><entry><title>X-planes: Are they needed in the new era of drones?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9q92x359xdo#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T23:03:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9q92x359xdo--c90d5a4dd6fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9q92x359xdo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Where do America's X-plane projects fit in an era of cheap drones?</summary></entry><entry><title>Why Australia chose the world's biggest political stage to reveal OpenAI hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr3eqk15ld14o#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:06:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr3eqk15ld14o--f912c18b19fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr3eqk15ld14o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Australia, which has strict social media restrictions and has proposed controls on algorithms and smart glasses, announced the breach at the UN.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rogue OpenAI agent 'infiltrated' Australian government website in world first</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6vgy0333dppo#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:42:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6vgy0333dppo--24a6d9427f52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6vgy0333dppo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Australia criticised OpenAI for taking "too long" to tell them about the breach which happened in June.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why did an OpenAI system hack Australia's health system - and can it be stopped in the future?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw24jm9rryy3o#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:08:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw24jm9rryy3o--f8a485533e9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw24jm9rryy3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">News that an automated AI agent hacked a government IT system raises big questions about regulating the tech.</summary></entry><entry><title>FBI investigating claim hackers have stolen details of all its agents</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9n74574elljo#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:23:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9n74574elljo--90aa3aaf99fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9n74574elljo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The hackers claim they have every agent's name, role, badge number and personal details including home address, phone numbers and spouse information.</summary></entry><entry><title>Are we back in big tech's 'move fast and break things' era?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6eq8egl3wd2o#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:29:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6eq8egl3wd2o--08be7c745599.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6eq8egl3wd2o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Despite promises to make safe AI, examples of bots behaving badly are now coming at us thick and fast.</summary></entry><entry><title>What you need to know about the OpenAI Australian government hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwe8ekyzdjvlo#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T05:18:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwe8ekyzdjvlo--45543d731f6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwe8ekyzdjvlo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The BBC’s North America technology correspondent Lily Jamali explains how the Medicare breach happened, and why it matters.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indians are discovering the thrill of shopping without paying</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwn741v5rdpxo#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T23:14:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwn741v5rdpxo--7ad5a0b3054d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwn741v5rdpxo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Dopamine sites mimic shopping’s thrill without the spending, turning the ritual of consumption into a digital game.</summary></entry><entry><title>US rejects pleas from OpenAI, Anthropic for global AI standards</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck87v27vdn1po#0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:11Z</u